<title>FRANCE: French January trade surplus 11.72 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>French January trade surplus 11.72 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>France had a seasonally adjusted trade surplus in January of 11.723 billion francs compared with a revised surplus in December of 8.528 billion, provisional customs office data showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The office had originally reported a surplus in December of 11.328 billion francs. The customs office said the revision was explained by the inclusion of French overseas departments.  </p>
<p>Detailed figures, in billions of francs and seasonally adjusted unless otherwise stated, were as follows:</p>
<p>					  Jan 97   Dec 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		     11.723    8.528</p>
<p> Trade balance (unadjusted)     6.422   10,946</p>
<p> Imports			    113.389  120,110</p>
<p> Exports			    125.112  128.638</p>
<p> Agri-business balance	    4.512    5,136</p>
<p> Energy balance		    -7.873   -8.855</p>
<p> Industrial/military balance   11.156    7.989</p>
<p> Airbus exports	3.109  (8 planes)  5.008 (11 planes)</p>
<p> Defence (unadj)		    0.547     2.896</p>
<p> Unadjusted exports	     122.761   128.952</p>
<p> Unadjusted imports	     116.339   118.006</p>
<p> European Union		     7.380     2.886</p>
<p> Germany				0.840     0.720</p>
<p> Japan				 -1.380    -1.626</p>
<p> United States		     -1.299    -3.212</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for 1996 came in at a revised 93.076 billion before seasonal adjustment versus 67.186 for 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 54 52</p>
